infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title When a CDN wins — and when it cannot
  desc The line is cacheability: shared bytes get edge-served, unique-per-user bytes still round-trip to origin
  compares
    - label Cacheable / shared content
      children
        - label Static assets — JS, CSS, images
          desc Identical for every user, so one cached copy serves all.
        - label Cache hit ratio 90-98%
          desc Most requests never touch origin once the edge is warm.
        - label 10-20x faster on a hit
          desc ~10-20 ms from the edge vs ~200-250 ms to origin.
        - label Origin sees under 10% of traffic
          desc Well-configured static site offloads the vast majority to edges.
    - label Personalised / unique content
      children
        - label Bank balance, feed, checkout total
          desc Different for every user — nothing shared to cache.
        - label Nothing to cache
          desc Each response must be fetched fresh from origin.
        - label Still a full origin round-trip
          desc Cache miss every time; proximity buys no caching win.
        - label Only TLS setup is saved
          desc Edge terminates TCP+TLS nearby, but the body comes from origin.
theme
  palette #10b981 #f43f5e
